3 Data and Task
WebNLG 2023 is the third iteration of the WebNLG shared task series and focuses on the severely under-resourced European languages Irish, Breton, Welsh and Maltese1 (Cripwell et al., 2023). The WebNLG 2023 data consists of 1,778 test items for each language, 1,399 dev items for Breton, and 1,665 dev items for Welsh, Irish and Maltese. The test sets were manually translated by professional translators from the English originals. Additionally 13,211 training items are provided where texts were automatically translated from English.
WebNLG 2023 systems map from RDF triples to a suitable output text, as in the example from the WebNLG’23 website2 in Figure 1. The complete shared-task data is available from the same website.
